WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:04.760
I'm Jenna Fisher.

2
00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:06.080
And I'm Angela Kinsey.

3
00:00:06.220 --> 00:00:07.360
We were on The Office together.

4
00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:08.620
And we're best friends.

5
00:00:08.680 --> 00:00:12.420
And now we're doing the Ultimate Office rewatch podcast just for you.

6
00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:19.420
Each week, we will break down an episode of The Office and give exclusive behind-the-scenes stories that only two people who were there can tell you.

7
00:00:19.580 --> 00:00:20.560
We're The Office Ladies.

8
00:00:23.590 --> 00:00:25.950
On your mark, get set, go.

9
00:00:26.930 --> 00:00:28.290
Angela, it's a fun run.

10
00:00:28.510 --> 00:00:32.610
Wait, I got a carb load, a bunch of fettuccine three seconds before I run.

11
00:00:33.590 --> 00:00:34.470
Good idea.

12
00:00:34.470 --> 00:00:36.550
Yeah, that's not going to turn on you.

13
00:00:37.550 --> 00:00:43.330
Give me the creamy carbs seconds before I take off on a huge adventure.

14
00:00:43.590 --> 00:00:46.150
Guys, it is fun run part two.

15
00:00:46.550 --> 00:00:53.310
This is the very beginning of season four, written by Greg Daniels, directed by Greg Daniels.

16
00:00:53.490 --> 00:00:55.090
Let me hit you up with a summary.

17
00:00:55.550 --> 00:01:00.290
Last week, Michael hit Meredith with his car, breaking her pelvis.

18
00:01:01.250 --> 00:01:02.890
And we discovered, though,

19
00:01:03.090 --> 00:01:11.990
that Meredith's trip to the hospital may have saved her life since it was revealed she had possibly been exposed to rabies and has now received a vaccine.

20
00:01:12.810 --> 00:01:17.210
We also found out that sprinkles died on Dwight's watch.

21
00:01:17.730 --> 00:01:19.430
On Dwight's watch?

22
00:01:20.050 --> 00:01:29.530
Well, this week, this week, Michael organizes a fun run to raise money for rabies in honor of Meredith.

23
00:01:29.630 --> 00:01:33.110
And we find out what really happened to sprinkles.

24
00:01:33.430 --> 00:01:36.590
Do you see what I'm wearing in honor of this episode?

25
00:01:37.090 --> 00:01:39.970
You're wearing your office lady's sprinkles sweatshirt.

26
00:01:40.070 --> 00:01:42.070
I am wearing my sprinkles sweatshirt.

27
00:01:42.230 --> 00:01:45.650
Well, lady, I did not wear anything in honor of sprinkles today.

28
00:01:45.790 --> 00:01:46.130
Well, you know what?

29
00:01:46.310 --> 00:01:48.670
That tracks for Pam in this episode.

30
00:01:48.670 --> 00:01:53.450
Because she helps, like, Angela, uh, uh, let's see, zero amount.

31
00:01:53.750 --> 00:01:54.330
Zero amount.

32
00:01:55.010 --> 00:01:55.610
Sorry.

33
00:01:55.950 --> 00:01:56.310
That's okay.

34
00:01:56.990 --> 00:02:02.210
She's distracted because in this episode, it's also going to be revealed that Jim and Pam are dating.

35
00:02:03.310 --> 00:02:10.410
Listen, one thing I thought of when I watched this episode was, wow, Happy Pam is a sassy Pam.

36
00:02:10.610 --> 00:02:14.030
She gives zero Fs about what's going on around her.

37
00:02:14.570 --> 00:02:16.030
She's a totally different person.

38
00:02:16.370 --> 00:02:17.290
Happy sass.

39
00:02:17.550 --> 00:02:18.470
Happy sass.

40
00:02:19.070 --> 00:02:20.090
Happy Pam sass.

41
00:02:20.410 --> 00:02:21.810
Happy Pam sass.

42
00:02:22.130 --> 00:02:24.430
Well, let's get into these fast facts.

43
00:02:24.570 --> 00:02:25.710
Fast fact number one.

44
00:02:25.930 --> 00:02:31.570
You know, this episode is technically the second part of the episode that we broke down last week, right?

45
00:02:31.990 --> 00:02:35.350
Because these episodes were an hour long.

46
00:02:35.490 --> 00:02:39.690
But if you notice, I feel like these episodes really stand on their own.

47
00:02:39.890 --> 00:02:43.670
They kind of both had their own little plots, right?

48
00:02:43.910 --> 00:02:44.290
For sure.

49
00:02:44.290 --> 00:02:53.310
Well, I talked to Greg about that, and he told me that Kevin Riley requested four hour-long episodes to kick off season four.

50
00:02:53.530 --> 00:02:58.230
So the first four episodes of this season are all an hour long.

51
00:02:58.230 --> 00:02:59.630
Kevin loved our show.

52
00:02:59.770 --> 00:03:03.390
But was there any other reason besides he was like, I want more office?

53
00:03:03.390 --> 00:03:13.790
I think it was just that would be a big announcement in the press, the return of the office, four hour-long episodes.

54
00:03:13.790 --> 00:03:18.610
Maybe also they didn't have something for the other time slot.

55
00:03:18.610 --> 00:03:21.150
So we were filling two time slots.

56
00:03:21.430 --> 00:03:22.450
I'm speculating.

57
00:03:22.450 --> 00:03:22.970
I don't know.

58
00:03:23.210 --> 00:03:26.410
I like your speculating face and tone.

59
00:03:26.850 --> 00:03:31.790
Because my husband does this sometimes when he wants to let the kids down easy.

60
00:03:32.150 --> 00:03:37.510
Like, it's like, hey, guys, so about those pumpkins that we were going to get.

61
00:03:37.950 --> 00:03:40.850
They exploded from the heat.

62
00:03:40.850 --> 00:03:42.570
But, yeah.

63
00:03:43.190 --> 00:03:46.690
Well, I was excited that we got these big, supersized episodes.

64
00:03:46.690 --> 00:03:51.330
It meant that for the supporting cast, some of our storylines would definitely stay in.

65
00:03:51.410 --> 00:03:52.330
And that was exciting.

66
00:03:53.470 --> 00:03:53.790
Yes.

67
00:03:54.350 --> 00:04:03.610
Well, Greg also told me that Kevin Riley told him they're only going to run in this hour-long length once at the beginning of the season.

68
00:04:03.610 --> 00:04:06.710
Then we're going to have to rerun them later as half hours.

69
00:04:07.410 --> 00:04:09.530
And that's really why they stand alone.

70
00:04:09.530 --> 00:04:20.890
Greg said it was a challenge because he had to wrap up the first episode in a way that would make it satisfying for a future viewer to watch it in a half-hour form.

71
00:04:21.010 --> 00:04:25.590
But he couldn't wrap it up too much for the people who were watching it as a one-hour episode.

72
00:04:25.650 --> 00:04:27.810
He said it was kind of a writing challenge.

73
00:04:28.370 --> 00:04:29.790
That sounds like a challenge.

74
00:04:30.130 --> 00:04:31.190
I think he did it, though.

75
00:04:31.350 --> 00:04:32.970
I think he crushed it.

76
00:04:33.190 --> 00:04:33.570
Greg Daniels.

77
00:04:34.530 --> 00:04:34.580
He crushed it.

78
00:04:34.580 --> 00:04:35.730
You crushed it.

79
00:04:35.730 --> 00:04:42.130
Fast fact number two, lady, is a wardrobe breakdown with Carrie Bennett.

80
00:04:42.350 --> 00:04:43.690
I love me some Carrie Bennett.

81
00:04:43.930 --> 00:04:44.490
Let's hear it.

82
00:04:45.130 --> 00:04:54.310
We got so much mail about the wardrobe in this episode, which makes sense because we're seeing everybody out of their office attire.

83
00:04:55.110 --> 00:05:00.950
Which Carrie said was always a challenge because she had created these office uniforms for people.

84
00:05:01.110 --> 00:05:07.790
So anytime we wore our, quote-unquote, street clothes, she was like, who are these people in their street clothes?

85
00:05:08.530 --> 00:05:10.070
Here's some of the mail we got.

86
00:05:10.570 --> 00:05:11.390
Alicia W.

87
00:05:11.730 --> 00:05:16.550
and Amanda Mitchenfelder said, did you get to keep your shirts from Fun Run?

88
00:05:16.550 --> 00:05:21.710
And Emily Thomas wants to know, did you get to keep a Support the Rabid wristband?

89
00:05:22.790 --> 00:05:24.310
Yeah, I kept both.

90
00:05:24.310 --> 00:05:26.650
I kept my shirt and I kept my wristband.

91
00:05:27.550 --> 00:05:29.990
I had my wristband for a long time.

92
00:05:30.010 --> 00:05:32.730
It's probably somewhere in my scrapbook bin.

93
00:05:33.130 --> 00:05:35.470
My t-shirt, I did not keep.

94
00:05:35.890 --> 00:05:45.230
Carrie kept it in case we ever needed Angela Martin to wear it again because we weren't sure how long this mourning process was going to go, you know?

95
00:05:45.850 --> 00:05:52.070
Well, we should remind people, Angela, you did not wear one of the famous blue Fun Run t-shirts.

96
00:05:52.350 --> 00:05:55.110
You wore a shirt with a picture of sprinkles on it.

97
00:05:55.250 --> 00:05:55.390
Yeah.

98
00:05:56.090 --> 00:05:58.070
Because people wrote in about this shirt too, Angela.

99
00:05:58.330 --> 00:05:58.870
Molly C.

100
00:05:59.090 --> 00:06:06.850
and Isaiah Johnson asked, where did Angela's sprinkle shirt come from and did you get to keep it?

101
00:06:06.930 --> 00:06:08.310
You said you did not keep it.

102
00:06:08.430 --> 00:06:09.650
I did not keep it.

103
00:06:10.070 --> 00:06:12.070
And Carrie made that shirt.

104
00:06:12.270 --> 00:06:13.310
She had that shirt made.

105
00:06:13.310 --> 00:06:18.250
And also when I had my wardrobe fitting for this, Carrie and I talked and Angela would not be in shorts.

106
00:06:18.790 --> 00:06:20.230
She would not wear shorts.

107
00:06:20.390 --> 00:06:22.650
So that's why I have sort of those little crop pants.

108
00:06:22.870 --> 00:06:30.470
And then at first they had kids for me and I was like, I can't run in kids and I have to actually run.

109
00:06:30.730 --> 00:06:33.090
So I need an actual sneaker.

110
00:06:33.370 --> 00:06:34.030
There you go.

111
00:06:34.150 --> 00:06:34.710
There you go.

112
00:06:34.930 --> 00:06:41.330
Well, Carrie told me about those blue shirts, the famous blue shirts with all the writing on them.

113
00:06:41.330 --> 00:06:44.770
So she designed those.

114
00:06:44.770 --> 00:06:45.970
We made them ourselves.

115
00:06:46.330 --> 00:06:58.370
She said that she just tried to imagine Michael getting on the phone and ordering those t-shirts with the ridiculously long name and insisting that all the words be on the shirt.

116
00:06:58.370 --> 00:07:02.090
Which I think is a very funny way to approach that design.

117
00:07:02.570 --> 00:07:04.350
I mean, I thought it was perfect.

118
00:07:04.650 --> 00:07:11.650
And honestly, while we're talking about the shirt, what the heck kind of budget did they have for this?

119
00:07:11.910 --> 00:07:16.790
Not only did they have bracelets and those t-shirts, they had flyers and banners.

120
00:07:16.790 --> 00:07:21.710
They had a giant Meredith photo poster and a giant check.

121
00:07:22.430 --> 00:07:23.630
What was their budget?

122
00:07:24.030 --> 00:07:31.570
I mean, we're going to see when we get to that scene in the conference room that we spend quite a bit of our donation money just throwing the fun run.

123
00:07:32.010 --> 00:07:38.750
Carrie also told me that she chose the color blue for the shirts because everybody had to wear it and blue looks good on everyone.

124
00:07:38.970 --> 00:07:43.010
She said she always applies the same logic for photo shoots and promo shoots.

125
00:07:43.390 --> 00:07:44.510
Blue just looks beSt.

126
00:07:44.750 --> 00:07:45.410
That's right.

127
00:07:45.410 --> 00:07:48.830
Well, let's talk about Dwight fan question from Ella Lewis.

128
00:07:49.610 --> 00:07:52.090
Why isn't Dwight wearing a fun run shirt?

129
00:07:52.290 --> 00:07:58.310
I feel like he would have been the most likely to support Michael's ideas, yet he's wearing a Shroot Farms shirt instead.

130
00:07:58.610 --> 00:08:01.870
I think it makes perfect sense that he would self-advertise.

131
00:08:02.070 --> 00:08:03.130
I agree with Ella.

132
00:08:03.370 --> 00:08:07.950
I was surprised that Dwight would not just champion Michael the way he does.

133
00:08:08.510 --> 00:08:10.670
Carrie told me that she made this shirt.

134
00:08:10.670 --> 00:08:18.950
She literally just used a standard stencil and she spray painted it in that parking lot right before we started shooting.

135
00:08:19.610 --> 00:08:21.390
But after the episode aired,

136
00:08:21.650 --> 00:08:30.950
NBC marketing department got so many requests for that shirt that they called her and asked her for her art files so that they could mass produce it and sell it.

137
00:08:31.130 --> 00:08:33.510
And Carrie was like, don't have an art file.

138
00:08:33.510 --> 00:08:37.890
Have a spray paint thing that I made in the parking lot.

139
00:08:38.330 --> 00:08:41.330
If you want to come get my spray paint stencil.

140
00:08:42.150 --> 00:08:42.550
Yeah.

141
00:08:43.010 --> 00:08:44.550
She was like, okay.

142
00:08:45.550 --> 00:08:46.370
All right.

143
00:08:46.450 --> 00:08:53.330
Well, our final question about the clothing comes from Ian MP and Marina Blank.

144
00:08:53.330 --> 00:08:58.110
They're asking, is Michael wearing women's shorts for Fun Run?

145
00:08:59.190 --> 00:09:00.130
Oh, man.

146
00:09:00.330 --> 00:09:05.630
They're definitely some kind of like biker short with like the little windbreaker short over it.

147
00:09:06.410 --> 00:09:06.630
Yeah.

148
00:09:07.290 --> 00:09:08.210
Carrie says no.

149
00:09:08.610 --> 00:09:10.430
They were not women's shorts.

150
00:09:10.810 --> 00:09:14.970
She said the thing with Steve was that he's actually really fit.

151
00:09:15.210 --> 00:09:16.990
And Angela, you and I know this.

152
00:09:17.130 --> 00:09:20.510
He was really, really into fitness.

153
00:09:20.950 --> 00:09:22.710
Well, he got into great shape.

154
00:09:22.710 --> 00:09:25.550
We've talked about that for 40-year-old Virgin.

155
00:09:25.810 --> 00:09:27.790
And then he has just made that part of his lifestyle.

156
00:09:28.170 --> 00:09:34.210
And I think in this episode, when he gets in his shorts and his t-shirt, you can see how fit he is.

157
00:09:34.330 --> 00:09:36.210
There's no hiding how fit he is.

158
00:09:36.370 --> 00:09:38.790
He has like 0% body fat.

159
00:09:38.970 --> 00:09:39.790
And it's very clear.

160
00:09:40.330 --> 00:09:46.930
Carrie said it was really a challenge to make him look like Michael anytime he was out of his sort of frumpy Michael suit.

161
00:09:47.310 --> 00:09:50.330
Because he just was in such great shape.

162
00:09:51.050 --> 00:09:52.930
She said it was just kind of difficult.

163
00:09:53.990 --> 00:09:55.150
So there you go.

164
00:09:56.050 --> 00:09:56.470
Yeah.

165
00:09:57.570 --> 00:10:00.470
That is a costume breakdown.

166
00:10:00.770 --> 00:10:01.710
I like it.

167
00:10:01.870 --> 00:10:02.150
Thank you so much.

168
00:10:02.370 --> 00:10:03.090
I like it.

169
00:10:03.390 --> 00:10:03.710
All right.

170
00:10:03.930 --> 00:10:05.230
Fast fact number three.

171
00:10:06.790 --> 00:10:10.730
As you know, in this episode, Jim and Pam do not run.

172
00:10:10.950 --> 00:10:12.130
A lot of people run.

173
00:10:13.390 --> 00:10:14.790
But Jim and Pam do not.

174
00:10:14.930 --> 00:10:15.550
They walk.

175
00:10:15.690 --> 00:10:16.970
They go to an estate sale.

176
00:10:17.510 --> 00:10:18.590
Jim and Pam don't run.

177
00:10:18.730 --> 00:10:22.610
And Oscar and Stanley and Creed take a cab.

178
00:10:22.750 --> 00:10:24.230
But Jim and Pam do not run.

179
00:10:24.550 --> 00:10:25.930
They walk in the back.

180
00:10:26.090 --> 00:10:27.050
They hold hands.

181
00:10:27.670 --> 00:10:29.450
Well, there was a reason for this.

182
00:10:29.750 --> 00:10:30.150
I know.

183
00:10:30.670 --> 00:10:36.930
The reason for this is because in May of 2007, we shot this in AuguSt.

184
00:10:36.930 --> 00:10:41.910
In May, I fell down a set of stairs in New York City.

185
00:10:42.110 --> 00:10:44.730
And I fractured four bones in my back.

186
00:10:45.370 --> 00:10:48.070
And I was not allowed to run.

187
00:10:48.070 --> 00:10:56.650
And so the writers had to write a reason for me to only walk through this episode.

188
00:10:57.250 --> 00:10:58.570
That was such a scary night.

189
00:10:58.750 --> 00:10:59.370
I was with you.

190
00:10:59.750 --> 00:11:00.950
I know you were.

191
00:11:01.170 --> 00:11:02.510
That was so scary.

192
00:11:02.930 --> 00:11:03.350
Yeah.

193
00:11:03.550 --> 00:11:04.610
So here's what happened.

194
00:11:05.330 --> 00:11:06.570
It was May.

195
00:11:06.570 --> 00:11:07.850
And we were in New York.

196
00:11:07.850 --> 00:11:09.510
And we were promoting the office.

197
00:11:09.510 --> 00:11:11.570
We were promoting the season finale.

198
00:11:11.950 --> 00:11:15.790
And they threw this big party, in quotes, party.

199
00:11:15.790 --> 00:11:18.830
It was a work event at this club called Budokan.

200
00:11:19.010 --> 00:11:19.130
Yeah.

201
00:11:19.210 --> 00:11:22.490
It was our job to kind of hobnob with advertisers and stuff.

202
00:11:22.610 --> 00:11:23.710
We were at work.

203
00:11:23.710 --> 00:11:25.510
But it was a fancy work.

204
00:11:26.030 --> 00:11:26.550
Yes.

205
00:11:26.810 --> 00:11:28.450
So we're all dressed up.

206
00:11:28.610 --> 00:11:31.590
And this club is two floors.

207
00:11:31.630 --> 00:11:33.490
So you enter on the upper floor.

208
00:11:33.670 --> 00:11:35.630
They had this little bar with drinks.

209
00:11:35.850 --> 00:11:40.510
And they were serving these, like, pineapple-y, daiquiri things.

210
00:11:41.130 --> 00:11:42.390
And it was sweet.

211
00:11:42.390 --> 00:11:43.990
And I was like, this seems great.

212
00:11:43.990 --> 00:11:45.150
So I grabbed one.

213
00:11:45.150 --> 00:11:50.190
But then to get to kind of the main part of the event, you had to go down this long set

214
00:11:50.190 --> 00:11:52.690
of stairs that were marble.

215
00:11:52.930 --> 00:11:54.350
And they were steep, you guys.

216
00:11:54.510 --> 00:11:57.130
They had a really deep pitch to them.

217
00:11:57.350 --> 00:11:57.630
Yeah.

218
00:11:57.710 --> 00:11:58.410
They're still there.

219
00:11:58.550 --> 00:11:59.570
This club is still there.

220
00:11:59.950 --> 00:12:01.610
So I'm walking down these stairs.

221
00:12:01.610 --> 00:12:03.310
I've basically just arrived.

222
00:12:03.470 --> 00:12:06.090
I've taken one sip of my little daiquiri.

223
00:12:06.710 --> 00:12:08.010
And something happens.

224
00:12:08.170 --> 00:12:10.250
My foot slips out from underneath me.

225
00:12:10.250 --> 00:12:14.030
And I go crashing down on the edge of these stairs hard.

226
00:12:14.030 --> 00:12:17.730
To add insult to injury, I also threw my drink in my own face.

227
00:12:18.230 --> 00:12:19.490
So that was fun.

228
00:12:19.490 --> 00:12:21.510
So I'm sitting on the ground.

229
00:12:21.630 --> 00:12:24.050
I'm half covered in daiquiri.

230
00:12:24.270 --> 00:12:30.210
And I immediately start to feel like I'm going to vomit or everything gets dizzy.

231
00:12:32.010 --> 00:12:36.410
And I remember this bouncer comes over and picked me up.

232
00:12:36.530 --> 00:12:43.350
And he was treating me like I was like a boozy, drunken Hollywood starlet.

233
00:12:43.910 --> 00:12:47.230
Like he was in no way regarding me with much care.

234
00:12:47.410 --> 00:12:48.510
It was like, get her out of there.

235
00:12:48.610 --> 00:12:49.650
Get the boozer out.

236
00:12:49.650 --> 00:12:55.050
And I was like, I'm not, I don't, but I was all disoriented, you know?

237
00:12:55.470 --> 00:12:59.190
So I remember they took me back to the storeroom, Angela, and you were there.

238
00:13:00.070 --> 00:13:02.070
And I told you I didn't feel good.

239
00:13:02.250 --> 00:13:05.850
And I remember you lifted up the back of my shirt.

240
00:13:06.950 --> 00:13:09.590
And you said, call an ambulance.

241
00:13:10.530 --> 00:13:14.330
Well, I was behind you on that staircase and I saw you go down.

242
00:13:14.330 --> 00:13:15.790
It happened in slow motion.

243
00:13:16.610 --> 00:13:21.070
And someone had spilt their drink or something on those stairs and they were marble and they

244
00:13:21.070 --> 00:13:21.830
were slick.

245
00:13:22.090 --> 00:13:27.190
And you, you had these wedge shoes on, you turned your ankle and you went down so hard.

246
00:13:27.310 --> 00:13:32.030
